# Design System Rules

## Multi-brand theming
- This is a multi-brand design system. The `THEME` env var (`kmart` | `target` or similar) determines which brand bundle is produced at compile time.
- Brand-specific tokens live in `src/configs/<brand>/tokens/` — palette, spacing, radius, breakpoints, typography, animation, and component-specific tokens.
- Raw hex/RGB values are BANNED outside config token files. Always reference tokens via the theme.
- Two separate builds ship as different package export subpaths (e.g. `.` for primary brand, `./<brand>` for secondary).

## ThemeWrapper pattern
- Every component wraps in a `<ThemeWrapper>` that injects the correct brand theme.
- `ThemeWrapper` detects whether a Kosmos theme is already in the React tree via a `__KOSMOS_brand` marker on the theme object. If present, it skips wrapping (avoids double-wrap).
- Never manually provide the MUI `ThemeProvider` in component code — always use `ThemeWrapper`.

## MUI v6 wrapper pattern
- Components wrap MUI components, restricting the API surface using `OmitKeys<MuiProps, ...>`.
- Expose a simpler, branded prop interface (e.g. `variant: "filled" | "outlined"` instead of MUI's full variant set).
- The MUI class prefix is `kosmos-ds-` to avoid style collisions with consumer apps.

## Component structure
- Components live at `src/components/ui/<category>/<component>/` with a standard 6-file structure:
  - `<Component>.tsx` — implementation
  - `<Component>.test.tsx` — unit tests
  - `<Component>.a11y.tsx` — accessibility tests (vitest-axe)
  - `<Component>.stories.tsx` — Storybook stories
  - `<Component>.mdx` — documentation
  - `index.ts` — barrel export
- A component is NOT public until exported from `src/components/ui/latest.ts`.

## Breaking changes
- Use version suffixes for breaking changes: `ButtonV3`, `CardV2` — not breaking existing APIs.
- Deprecated components remain available but marked with `@deprecated` JSDoc and console warnings in dev.
- Never remove a public component without a migration guide and at least one major version notice.

## Strict code quality
- ESLint enforces: complexity ≤ 8, max-statements ≤ 10, max-depth ≤ 3.
- If your code exceeds these limits, decompose it into smaller functions or components. Do not disable the rule.
- Prefer composition (children, slots, render props) over complex conditional rendering.

## Bundling
- tsup (esbuild) bundles the library. Every entry point includes a `"use client"` banner for Next.js RSC compatibility.
- Do not use Node.js-only APIs (fs, path, etc.) in component code — it must run in both server and client contexts.
- Tree-shaking must work: use named exports, avoid side effects at module scope.

## Available libraries
- **Radix UI** (`@radix-ui/react-select`) — headless primitives for complex interactions (select, dropdown). Use when MUI's component doesn't fit or needs deeper customization.
- **lucide-react** — standard icon set. Use for generic icons. Brand-specific icons go in `src/components/ui/custom-icons/`.
- **embla-carousel-react** — carousel/slider engine. Used by carousel components.
- **Emotion** (`@emotion/styled`, `@emotion/react`, `@emotion/cache`) — MUI's styling engine. Direct usage is fine for component styling alongside `sx`.

## Plop scaffolding
- Use `pnpm plop` to generate new components with the standard 6-file template.
- The Plop generator ensures consistent naming, directory structure, and boilerplate.
- After scaffolding, add the component export to `src/components/ui/latest.ts` once it's ready for consumers.

## Testing
- **Unit tests** (`*.test.tsx`): Use `@testing-library/react` with `userEvent`. Vitest globals enabled (no imports for `describe`, `test`, `expect`, `vi`).
- **A11y tests** (`*.a11y.tsx`): Separate file using `vitest-axe`. Every component must have one.
- **Emotion test helper**: Wrap renders in `withEmotion()` from `src/utils/test-helper/emotion-query.tsx` for inspectable styles. Call `cleanUpEmotionStyles()` in `afterEach`.
- `vitest.setup.js` mocks `window.matchMedia`, `IntersectionObserver`, `ResizeObserver`, and `HTMLCanvasElement.getContext`.

## Theming — never hardcode
- Pull design values from the theme via `sx` prop, `styled()`, or `useTheme()`.
- Spacing uses the theme spacing scale (`theme.spacing(n)` / `sx` shorthand).
- Add new colors/typography/radii as tokens in the brand config, then reference them.

## Variants & styling
- Implement visual variants through theme `components[X].variants` and `styleOverrides`.
- Expose variants as a typed `variant` prop (string union).
- Tailwind CSS 3.4 is available alongside Emotion for utility styling — prefer theme tokens where possible.

## Refs & controlled components
- Apply `forwardRef` to every interactive or focusable component.
- Forward the ref to the underlying DOM node. Type it explicitly (`forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, ButtonProps>`).
- Support both controlled (`value` + `onChange`) and uncontrolled (`defaultValue`) modes.

## Prop API
- Keep prop APIs clear, minimal, and well-typed. Prefer composition over configuration.
- Prefer `variant`/`size`/`color` unions over boolean flags.
- Extend underlying element props (`React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<'button'>`) so consumers can pass `aria-*`, `data-*`, `id`.
- Provide sensible defaults for the common case.

## Stories
- One Storybook story file per component, co-located.
- Use CSF3 (`Meta` / `StoryObj`), `tags: ['autodocs']`.
- Cover all states: default, hover/focus, loading, error, disabled, empty, and each brand variant.
- Storybook 10 with `@storybook/nextjs` framework.

## Accessibility
- Correct semantic roles and accessible names on every interactive element.
- Full keyboard operability with visible focus indicators.
- Meet WCAG 2.2 AA (contrast, target size, focus-not-obscured). See the `wcag-2.2-aa` skill.
- vitest-axe must pass for each component's a11y test file.

## Public API
- Export through `src/components/ui/latest.ts` (the public barrel). Only export consumer-ready components.
- Export component types alongside components (`export type { ButtonProps }`).
- Keep internals out of the public barrel.

## Versioning
- semantic-release with Conventional Commits: `feat(button):`, `fix(theme):`, etc.
- BREAKING CHANGE footer triggers major version bump.
- Publish to GitHub Packages as `@kmartau/kosmos-ds.react-components` (or the configured scope).
